<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Cross Modal Prototype Alignment</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While CDCR and DAR operate in the prediction space, learning domain-invariant and cross-modally consistent features is crucial for multimodal domain generalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>.
To this end, we propose Cross-Modal Prototype Alignment (CMPA), which aligns features with both intra-domain class prototypes and corresponding prototypes from other modalities and domains.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We maintain running-average class-prototypes <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{m,c}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{m,c}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> for each modality <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{v,a\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{v,a\}</annotation></semantics></math>, class <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and domain <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. These are updated via exponential moving average (EMA) using the set <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{m,c}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{m,c}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as the set of labeled features <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> from the current batch belonging to modality <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, class <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, and domain <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{m,c}^{(k)}\leftarrow\alpha\bm{\mu}_{m,c}^{(k)}+(1-\alpha)\cdot\frac{1}{|\mathcal{F}_{m,c}^{(k)}|}\sum_{\mathbf{f}_{m}\in\mathcal{F}_{m,c}^{(k)}}\mathbf{f}_{m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{m,c}^{(k)}\leftarrow\alpha\bm{\mu}_{m,c}^{(k)}+(1-\alpha)\cdot\frac{1}{|\mathcal{F}_{m,c}^{(k)}|}\sum_{\mathbf{f}_{m}\in\mathcal{F}_{m,c}^{(k)}}\mathbf{f}_{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is the momentum. To facilitate cross-modal alignment and enable robustness to missing modalities, we introduce modality translators <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{v\to a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{v\to a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{a\to v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{a\to v}</annotation></semantics></math> that map features from one modality to another: <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{a}^{j}=t_{v\to a}(\mathbf{z}_{v}^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{a}^{j}=t_{v\to a}(\mathbf{z}_{v}^{j})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{v}^{j}=t_{a\to v}(\mathbf{z}_{a}^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{v}^{j}=t_{a\to v}(\mathbf{z}_{a}^{j})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{w,s\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{w,s\}</annotation></semantics></math>. These translators not only support alignment but also handle missing-modality scenarios at inference by synthesizing a missing feature from a present one <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. For example, if the audio feature is missing, it is synthesized from the video feature via the translator <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{v\to a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{v\to a}</annotation></semantics></math> (and vice versa).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For all pseudo-labeled unlabeled samples <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}\in\mathcal{B}^{u}=\mathcal{B}^{u}_{\text{cdcr}}\cup\mathcal{B}^{u}_{\text{dar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext>cdcr</mtext><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext>dar</mtext><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}\in\mathcal{B}^{u}=\mathcal{B}^{u}_{\text{cdcr}}\cup\mathcal{B}^{u}_{\text{dar}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we align both original and translated features to intra-domain prototypes <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> and cross-domain averages <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{\mu}}_{m,\hat{y}}^{-k}=\frac{1}{K-1}\sum_{k^{\prime}\neq k}\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{\mu}}_{m,\hat{y}}^{-k}=\frac{1}{K-1}\sum_{k^{\prime}\neq k}\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> using:</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{align}}(\mathbf{z},\bm{\mu},\bar{\bm{\mu}})=\|\mathbf{z}-\bm{\mu}\|_{2}^{2}+\|\mathbf{z}-\bar{\bm{\mu}}\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>align</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{align}}(\mathbf{z},\bm{\mu},\bar{\bm{\mu}})=\|\mathbf{z}-\bm{\mu}\|_{2}^{2}+\|\mathbf{z}-\bar{\bm{\mu}}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The total prototype loss is:</p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\mathcal{L}_{\text{cmpa}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{u}|}\sum_{\bm{U}\in\mathcal{B}^{u}}\sum_{j\in\{w,s\}}\sum_{m\in\{v,a\}}\bigg[\\
&amp;\quad\mathcal{L}_{\text{align}}(\mathbf{z}_{m}^{j},\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k)},\bar{\bm{\mu}}_{m,\hat{y}}^{-k})+\quad\mathcal{L}_{\text{align}}(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{m}^{j},\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k)},\bar{\bm{\mu}}_{m,\hat{y}}^{-k})\bigg].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>cmpa</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>align</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.222em">+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>align</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\mathcal{L}_{\text{cmpa}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{u}|}\sum_{\bm{U}\in\mathcal{B}^{u}}\sum_{j\in\{w,s\}}\sum_{m\in\{v,a\}}\bigg[\\
&amp;\quad\mathcal{L}_{\text{align}}(\mathbf{z}_{m}^{j},\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k)},\bar{\bm{\mu}}_{m,\hat{y}}^{-k})+\quad\mathcal{L}_{\text{align}}(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{m}^{j},\bm{\mu}_{m,\hat{y}}^{(k)},\bar{\bm{\mu}}_{m,\hat{y}}^{-k})\bigg].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Overall Objective</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For labeled samples in batch <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply standard supervision:</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{sup}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{l}|}\sum_{(\bm{X},y)\in\mathcal{B}^{l}}\sum_{n\in\{v,a,f\}}\mathcal{H}(y,\hat{\mathbf{p}}^{l}_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>sup</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{sup}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{l}|}\sum_{(\bm{X},y)\in\mathcal{B}^{l}}\sum_{n\in\{v,a,f\}}\mathcal{H}(y,\hat{\mathbf{p}}^{l}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The overall objective is:</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{L}_{\text{cdcr}}+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{dar}}+\lambda_{3}\mathcal{L}_{\text{cmpa}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>sup</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cdcr</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>dar</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cmpa</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{L}_{\text{cdcr}}+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{L}_{\text{dar}}+\lambda_{3}\mathcal{L}_{\text{cmpa}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\lambda_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\lambda_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are hyperparameters. This objective is designed to leverage both labeled and unlabeled data while promoting robust cross-domain and cross-modal generalization.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SSMDG results on the HAC dataset with 10, 5%, and 10% labels per class. We report the mean accuracy across all domains.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:496.9pt;height:228pt;vertical-align:-111.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(10.0pt,-4.6pt) scale(1.041836114765,1.041836114765) ;">
<table id="S4.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modality</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5%</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10%</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">Video</th>
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">Audio</th>
<th id="S4.T2.5.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">Flow</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">CGMatch<sup id="S4.T2.5.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">M</span></sup> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">59.33</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">58.74</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.3.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">59.32</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">STiL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.4.4" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">60.66</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">58.96</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">60.21</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">NIED-LR<sup id="S4.T2.5.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">M</span></sup> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.4" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">62.92</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">61.08</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">62.86</td></tr>
